WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.060
In 1776, Adam Smith described a
small workshop that made pins.

2
00:00:06.060 --> 00:00:07.330
One worker on their own,

3
00:00:07.330 --> 00:00:11.470
he wrote, certainly could not
make twenty pins in a day.

4
00:00:11.470 --> 00:00:16.740
Yet ten workers in that workshop
made upwards of 48,000 pins a day.

5
00:00:16.740 --> 00:00:19.900
That is about 4,800 each.

6
00:00:19.900 --> 00:00:23.410
So how could ten workers
make thousands of pins a day,

7
00:00:23.410 --> 00:00:26.150
when one alone could barely make twenty?

8
00:00:26.150 --> 00:00:28.590
In this mission, you'll measure
what a change in the way

9
00:00:28.590 --> 00:00:33.320
work is organised does to output
per worker and cost per unit.

10
00:00:33.320 --> 00:00:35.190
Then you'll weigh the downsides,

11
00:00:35.190 --> 00:00:37.580
and see why specialists have to trade,

12
00:00:37.580 --> 00:00:39.350
and how money helps.

13
00:00:39.350 --> 00:00:43.000
Your mission: find out where
all those extra pins came from.
